instruction:
Given the ellipse \(\frac{x^{2}}{6}+\frac{y^{2}}{2}=1\) with the right focus at \(F\), a line passing through \(F\) of the form \(y=k(x-2)(k \neq 0)\) intersects the ellipse at points \(P\) and \(Q\). If the midpoint of \(PQ\) is \(N\), \(O\) is the origin, and the line \(ON\) intersects the line \(x=3\) at point \(M\), find:
(1) The measure of \(\angle M F Q\);
(2) The maximum value of \(\frac{P Q}{M F}\).

In right triangle $JKL$, angle $J$ measures 60 degrees and angle $K$ measures 30 degrees. When drawn, the angle bisectors of angles $J$ and $K$ intersect at a point $M$. What is the measure of obtuse angle $JMK$?

[asy]
import geometry;
import olympiad;
unitsize(0.8inch);
dotfactor = 3;
defaultpen(linewidth(1pt)+fontsize(10pt));

pair J,K,L,M,U,V;

J = (0,0);
K = (1,2);
L = (1,0);

draw(J--K--L--cycle);
draw(rightanglemark(J,L,K,5));

label("$J$",J,W);
label("$K$",K,N);
label("$L$",L,E);

U = (1,2/3);
V = (2/(2+sqrt(3)),0);

draw(J--U);
draw(K--V);

M = intersectionpoint(J--U,K--V);
dot("M",M,NW);
[/asy]

Find all monotonic functions \( f: \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R} \) such that 
\[ f(-a^3 + b^3 + c^3) + f(a^3 - b^3 + c^3) + f(a^3 + b^3 - c^3) + 24f(abc) = f(a^3 + b^3 + c^3) \]
for all \( a, b, c \in \mathbb{R}. \)

Given an ellipse $\Omega$, find:
(1) The maximum area of a triangle inscribed in $\Omega$;
(2) The minimum area of a triangle circumscribed about $\Omega$.
